│ ★  Owner       Name        Private                           ││                         LazyGithub: A Terminal UI For GitHub (0.1.0)                         │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0500  ✘                               ▆▆││                                                                                              │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0501  ✘                                 ││  LazyGithub is a terminal UI for interacting with GitHub. You can get started by selecting   │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0502  ✘                                 ││  one of the repositories listed in the table on the left. Once you have selected a           │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0503  ✘                                 ││  repository, any issues, pull requests, and action workflows will be retrieved and           │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0504  ✘                                 ││  displayed below it.                                                                         │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0505  ✘                                 ││                                                                                              │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0506  ✘                                 ││  Issues, pull requests, and action lists can also be interacted with!                        │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0507  ✘                                 ││                                                                                              │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0508  ✘                                 ││                                                                                              │
│ ☆  parity-bot  large-0509  ✘                                 ││  Pull Requests                                                                               │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘│                                                                                              │
┌─ [2] Pull Requests ──────────────────────────────────────────┐│  You can interact with a PR by viewing its details, viewing the PR diff, and participating   │
│ #  Status  Author  Title                                     ││  in any active conversations happening on the PR. You can also create a new PR for the       │
│                                                              ││  currently selected repo.                                                                    │
│                                                              ││                                                                                              │
│                                                              ││                                                                                              │
│                                                              ││  Issues                                                                                      │
│                                                              ││                                                                                              │
│                                                              ││  You can interact with an issue by viewing its details, partipcating in any activate         │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘│  conversations happening on the issue, and by editing the issue itself. This means that you  │
┌─ [3] Issues ─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐│  can close an issue from within LazyGithub.                                                  │
│ #  Status  Author  Title                                     ││                                                                                              │
│                                                              ││                                                                                              │
│                                                              ││  Actions                                                                                     │
│                                                              ││                                                                                              │
│                                                              ││  Github action and workflow support is pretty limited. It currently only supports listing    │
│                                                              ││  the workflows and the most recent runs across all actions on the currently selected repo,   │
│                                                              ││  as well as kicking off a workflow that supports manual triggers.                            │
